# Spyglass Siren: a flying 1/1 that creates a Map token when it enters (CR 111.10s), and only then (attacking makes
# no second Map). On turn 3 it attacks past Bot2's Llanowar Elves (a ground creature cannot block a flyer, so the
# attack deals 1), then in main 2 the Map ({1}, {T}, sacrifice, sorcery speed) makes the Siren explore (CR 701.44):
# the revealed Lightning Bolt is not a land, so the Siren gets a +1/+1 counter and the Bolt may go to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Spyglass Siren
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Llanowar Elves
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spyglass Siren.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Spyglass Siren; Map Token
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Attack(Spyglass Siren > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Spyglass Siren; Map Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Map Token.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Spyglass Siren)
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Spyglass Siren
Bot1.Battlefield.Spyglass Siren.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
